From: Domenico D'Arrigo <DCHEM88@hotmail.it>
Date: Thu, 1 Oct 2026 20:05:25 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] mb/lenovo/haswell: Report hotkeys like the OEM firmware

The OEM firmware of the W541 (GNETxxWW) ignores EC event 0x11, reports
event 0x12 as HKEY 0x1002, and reports events 0x66 to 0x69 (Fn-F9 to
Fn-F12) as HKEY 0x101d to 0x1020. coreboot uses the default H8 layout,
which reports 0x11 and 0x12 as 0x1002 and 0x1003, 0x66 and 0x67 as
0x100a and 0x1013, and ignores 0x68 and 0x69.

Select the alternative Fn-F2/F3 layout and the Fn-F9 to Fn-F12 layout,
which match the OEM firmware for these events.

TEST=Built for W541 and T440p, and checked the _Q11, _Q12 and _Q66 to
_Q69 methods in the DSDT. Not tested on hardware yet.

Co-authored-by: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_018n3yuWwDLW63F4vdf7ZFTv
---
 src/mainboard/lenovo/haswell/dsdt.asl | 2 ++
 1 file changed, 2 insertions(+)

diff --git a/src/mainboard/lenovo/haswell/dsdt.asl b/src/mainboard/lenovo/haswell/dsdt.asl
index 046584a87..70d13de92 100644
--- a/src/mainboard/lenovo/haswell/dsdt.asl
+++ b/src/mainboard/lenovo/haswell/dsdt.asl
@@ -4,6 +4,8 @@
 #define BRIGHTNESS_DOWN \_SB.PCI0.GFX0.DECB
 #define THINKPAD_EC_GPE 17
 #define THINKPAD_EC_WAKE_GPE 0x1d /* GPIO13 */
+#define EC_LENOVO_H8_ALT_FN_F2F3_LAYOUT 1
+#define EC_LENOVO_H8_FN_F9_F12_LAYOUT 1
 
 #include <acpi/acpi.h>
 DefinitionBlock(
